{"oil":{"id":"f7c537a8-7e17-4941-9691-78d6a4a382bf","word":"oil","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"lubricate with oil","word":"olear"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to grease with oil for cooking","word":"olear"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Before they went to see Glinda, however, they were taken to a room of the Castle, where Dorothy washed her face and combed her hair, and the Lion shook the dust out of his mane, and the Scarecrow patted himself into his best shape, and the Woodman polished his tin and oiled his joints.","ref":"1900 May 17, L[yman] Frank Baum, chapter 23, in The Wonderful Wizard of Oz, Chicago, Ill.; New York, N.Y.: Geo[rge] M[elvin] Hill Co., →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[269,274]],"id":"55bdfaa2-cfa7-40f1-8ee8-b6c72ba0d36c"},{"text":"Platform faces in Holland are further back from the track than they are in Britain, and it is a common thing to see a driver standing quite comfortably between his engine and the platform while oiling the motion.","ref":"1955 February, E. J. Tyler and J. Quanjer, “The Steam Locomotive in Holland 1919-1954”, in Railway Magazine, page 131:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[194,200]],"id":"fa644964-0e25-4e7f-b046-fae1e3ffadd1"},{"text":"The face which emerged was not reassuring.[…]. He was not a mongol but there was a deficiency of a sort there, and it was not made more pretty by a latter-day hair cut which involved eccentrically long elf-locks and oiled black curls.","ref":"1963, Margery Allingham, chapter 17, in The China Governess: A Mystery, London: Chatto & Windus, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[216,221]],"id":"29072571-48b3-4208-af49-9dda193b13b5"}],"categories":["English links with manual fragments","English terms with quotations","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["lubricate","lubricate"]],"hypernyms":[{"word":"lubricate"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"grease"}],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To lubricate with oil."],"glosses":["To lubricate with oil."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"ca3fb7a1-62d4-4775-a689-b3dc6f07a8a4"},{"categories":["English transitive verbs"],"links":[["grease","grease"],["cook","cook"]],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To grease with oil for cooking."],"glosses":["To grease with oil for cooking."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"9010825a-4805-420a-b56c-2dff8a9e2239"},{"categories":["English transitive verbs"],"links":[["fuel","fuel"]],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To fuel with oil."],"glosses":["To fuel with oil."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"d48dd2a2-a6ba-4dde-b09b-d911b932240f"},{"examples":[{"text":"\"Do you need a drink?\" oils Robert Ryan to the disinterested Stanwyck in Clash By Night; \"Let's say that's what I need,\" she sneers back.","ref":"1984 December 22, Michael Bronski, “Women Act Out on Film”, in Gay Community News, volume 12, number 23, page 10:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,27]],"id":"d296b6bc-684c-4394-9067-f02653b47f43"}],"categories":["English idioms","English intransitive verbs","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["say","say"],["unctuous","unctuous"],["manner","manner"]],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive, idiomatic) To say in an unctuous manner."],"glosses":["To say in an unctuous manner."],"tags":["idiomatic","intransitive"],"id":"31e400f0-ffa1-439a-be2d-2e2aea1bce53"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"oily":{"id":"8ff64190-6d47-4315-8037-eda87e54d5f6","word":"oily","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"relating to oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleoso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"relating to oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleaginoso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"relating to oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleento"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"covered with or containing oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleoso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"covered with or containing oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleaginoso"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"covered with or containing oil","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oleento"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"oily machinery;   oily rags;   oily fish;   oily cooking","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4],[18,22],[31,35],[44,48]],"type":"example","id":"7453bfb9-0bba-4142-83a1-237ee11759c6"},{"text":"His clothes were apt to look oily and smell of eating-houses.","ref":"1853, Herman Melville, Bartleby, the Scrivener:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[29,33]],"id":"2aa0a918-ac61-4117-9147-b99db9adff69"},{"text":"[…] overdressed young men of enigmatic appearance, with oily thick hair, shifty eyes, and hands covered with cheap rings, swaggered about smoking cigarettes and talking in loud, ostentatious voices.","ref":"1917, Robert Hichens, Wilderness, Chapter:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,60]],"id":"5269a413-077b-4170-bb93-1b818499fe18"},{"text":"Dyes listed with the word “lake” indicate the dye is a fat-soluble version, meaning it can dissolve in oily foods or drinks.","ref":"2025 March 29, Kristen Rogers, “Over half of US states are trying to eliminate food dyes. Here’s what you can do now”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[103,107]],"id":"69e667db-ad53-4d29-bdac-e3b6aef67f88"}],"senseid":["en:covered with or containing oil"],"links":[["oil","oil"]],"categories":["English terms with collocations","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Covered with or containing oil."],"id":"77804351-2499-4701-a9ad-8f00df43fac7"},{"examples":[{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"oily swells;   oily seas","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4],[15,19]],"type":"example","id":"bb45ba71-d007-49b5-8224-ed80fbcb082f"},{"text":"There were no breakers and no waves, for not a breath of wind was stirring. Only a slight oily swell rose and fell like a gentle breathing, and showed that the eternal sea was still moving and living.","ref":"1895 May 29, H[erbert] G[eorge] Wells, “After the Story”, in The Time Machine: An Invention, London: William Heinemann, →OCLC, page 195:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[90,94]],"id":"cc73c908-49de-455a-84ef-9b40730c7202"}],"senseid":["en:resembling oil"],"links":[["oil","oil"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"oilish"},{"word":"oillike"}],"categories":["English terms with collocations","English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Resembling oil."],"id":"f0d0851f-5677-4cc1-81a2-6d772016ab83"},{"examples":[{"text":"Near-synonyms: slick, buttery; smarmy","id":"09abe3fe-030b-43d1-be01-72ac6f4d1d8d"},{"text":"[…] for I want that glib and oyly Art,\nTo ſpeake and purpoſe not, ſince what I well entend\nIle do’t before I ſpeake, […]","ref":"c. 1603–1606 (date written), [William Shakespeare], […] His True Chronicle Historie of the Life and Death of King Lear and His Three Daughters. […] (First Quarto), London: […] Nathaniel Butter, […], published 1608, →OCLC, [Act I, scene i]:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[29,33]],"id":"bbb01136-3090-49d8-9de9-56c5cd2648b0"},{"text":"Mr. Carker the Manager, sly of manner, sharp of tooth, soft of foot, watchful of eye, oily of tongue, cruel of heart, nice of habit, sat with a dainty stedfastness and patience at his work, as if he were waiting at a mouse’s hole.","ref":"1846 October 1 – 1848 April 1, Charles Dickens, “A Trifle of Management by Mr. Carker the Manager”, in Dombey and Son, London: Bradbury and Evans, […], published 1848, →OCLC, page 211:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[86,90]],"id":"0eaa1b53-7693-466e-b4a5-62af20cd46e3"},{"text":"‘He had an inflexible will beneath all that oily kindness which passed for spiritual […]’","ref":"1914, Algernon Blackwood, The Damned:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,48]],"id":"8f3d7a7f-78ec-41f6-a573-3dcd37a056fd"}],"senseid":["en:excessively friendly or polite but insincere"],"links":[["friendly","friendly"],["polite","polite"],["insincere","insincere"]],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"soapy"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"slick"},{"word":"buttery"},{"word":";"},{"word":"smarmy"}],"categories":["English links with manual fragments","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"raw_glosses":["(figuratively) Excessively friendly or polite but insincere."],"glosses":["Excessively friendly or polite but insincere."],"tags":["figuratively"],"id":"d44ea517-aa5d-4917-86e6-40f2986cd11b"}],"related":[{"word":"oilfish"},{"word":"oilseed"},{"word":"olive-oily"}],"synonyms":[]},"oil field":{"id":"6af79c60-74fd-43c4-924f-fb317d962106","word":"oil field","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"area under which are reserves of petroleum","tags":["masculine"],"word":"campo de petróleo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"area under which are reserves of petroleum","tags":["masculine"],"word":"campo petrolífero"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Too many puppies are being shot in the dark\nToo many puppies are trained not to bark\nAt the sight of blood that must be spilled so that we may maintain our oil fields","ref":"1990, “Too Many Puppies”, performed by Primus:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[156,166]],"id":"941dc12b-6fce-47d2-9700-fa6d5ba9a172"}],"links":[["area","area"],["reserve","reserve"],["petroleum","petroleum"],["productive","productive"],["oil well","oil well"]],"categories":["Cantonese terms with redundant transliterations","English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English nouns","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Cantonese translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Estonian translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Norwegian Nynorsk translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations"],"glosses":["An area under which are reserves of petroleum, especially one with productive oil wells."],"id":"8801f8b6-3421-4712-aedf-3f13253d28d2"}],"related":[{"word":"gas field"}],"synonyms":[]},"oil painting":{"id":"27930f9d-f80f-4de2-b2ee-d745fb31f94c","word":"oil painting","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a painting done with oil paints","tags":["feminine"],"word":"pintura a óleo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a painting done with oil paints","tags":["masculine"],"word":"óleo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"art of painting with oil paints","tags":["feminine"],"word":"pintura a óleo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["painting","painting"],["oil paint","oil paint"]],"glosses":["A painting done with oil paints."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"4262a24f-4601-4f85-adf3-016bcf55f1ee"},{"categories":["English uncountable nouns"],"links":[["art","art"]],"raw_glosses":["(uncountable) The art of painting with oil paints."],"glosses":["The art of painting with oil paints."],"tags":["uncountable"],"id":"b7e2d8eb-de05-4641-8e74-e7a7996e97f4"},{"examples":[{"text":"\"Very lovely!\" he said, staring her straight in the face.\n\"You needn't try and be funny!\" she said. \"If you mean me, I'm no oil-painting, and I know it!\"","ref":"1920, Henry St. John Cooper, “Sunny Ducrow”, in Putnam's, page 117:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[124,136]],"id":"04ab07e8-fc8e-49f1-9d60-d08e2e6d2464"},{"text":"Wayne Swan: All I can say is that she's a much more attractive person than the Prime Minister.\nGeorge Brandis: You're not exactly an oil painting yourself, Wayne.","ref":"2007 \"Virginia Trioli talks to George Brandis and Wayne Swan\" Lateline ABC (Australia) 14 September 2007","id":"7194afd4-2016-474a-a3f4-bd6b367e2e4a"}],"categories":["British English","English humorous terms","English litotes","English negative polarity items","English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(British, humorous, litotes, chiefly in the negative) A physically attractive person."],"glosses":["A physically attractive person."],"tags":["British","countable","humorous","uncountable"],"raw_tags":["in the negative"],"id":"837a71d9-56f0-4f3c-88ac-31b5fa237852"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"oil well":{"id":"9359acd7-9f26-448a-99dc-2b291f0250b4","word":"oil well","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"hole drilled into the earth from which petroleum is pumped","tags":["masculine"],"word":"poço de petróleo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["hole","hole"],["drilled","drilled"],["earth","earth"],["petroleum","petroleum"],["pumped","pumped"]],"glosses":["A hole drilled into the earth from which petroleum is pumped."],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Belarusian translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Cantonese translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Georgian translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Iranian Persian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Marathi translations","Terms with Māori translations","Terms with Navajo translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Tagalog translations","Terms with Tamil translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations"],"id":"66bf9cea-bf56-4ae6-89ca-6490c4ab9528"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"oil shale":{"id":"fbd2a1e9-6e9b-48bc-b782-c0e1e5460fc5","word":"oil shale","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"shale from which hydrocarbons can be produced","tags":["masculine"],"word":"xisto betuminoso"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Up in the mountains along both sides of Parachute Creek the Exxon Corporation and other companies have begun to pour billions of dollars into two huge projects to turn the nation's immense reserves of oil shale into shale oil.","ref":"1981 November 6, Robert D. Hershey Jr, “Shale Oil Is Coming Of Age”, in The New York Times, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[201,210]],"id":"3bc5d4dd-3076-41e6-8136-3e5fd4311c5d"},{"text":"Can you imagine squeezing oil from rock? Oil shale is different from the shale gas that is extracted through fracking. It is geologically un-evolved oil: the remnants of organic matter buried underground for millions of years but never sunk deep enough, nor long enough, to be transformed into petroleum.","ref":"2014 April 16, Martin Lukacs, “Canada becoming launch-pad of a global tar sands and oil shale frenzy”, in The Guardian:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[41,50]],"id":"904251ce-d5a9-4677-9548-4bb47c3961f0"}],"links":[["sedimentary rock","sedimentary rock"],["kerogen","kerogen"],["petroleum","petroleum"],["like","like"],["shale oil","shale oil"],["produce","produce"],["pyrolysis","pyrolysis"],["hydrogenation","hydrogenation"]],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English nouns","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Estonian translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Icelandic translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Norwegian Nynorsk translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Thai translations","en:Geology","en:Petroleum"],"glosses":["A sedimentary rock containing kerogen from which petroleum-like shale oil can be produced by pyrolysis, hydrogenation, or thermal dissolution."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"0a31b0bd-2508-472c-8f73-02fb8afacece"}],"related":[{"word":"shale oil"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"kerogen shale"}]},"oil sand":{"id":"97a1407d-1613-428d-8f04-4d2bca93b063","word":"oil sand","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"relatively loose sandstone or porous carbonate rock impregnated with bitumen","tags":["feminine"],"word":"areia betuminosa"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["sandstone","sandstone"],["porous","porous"],["carbonate","carbonate"],["rock","rock"],["impregnate","impregnate"],["bitumen","bitumen"]],"glosses":["A relatively loose sandstone, or porous carbonate rock, impregnated with bitumen."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"categories":["En